- name: link_layer
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "\"\"\"GNU Radio shim for the BPSK network node (r6.1: FDMA mesh)\
      \ and chat app.\n\nThese files must sit in the same directory as the flowgraph:\n\
      \n    bpsk_link.py    framing, addressing, Selective Repeat ARQ, file segmentation\n\
      \    bpsk_mac.py     channel and address self-assignment, beacons\n    bpsk_secure.py\
      \  end-to-end encryption: Noise KK sessions, sealing\n    bpsk_crypto.py  ChaCha20-Poly1305\
      \ / X25519 (pure Python or 'cryptography')\n    bpsk_gain.py    closed-loop\
      \ gain staging (RX gain, TX attenuation)\n    bpsk_phy.py     deframer, transmit\
      \ framer, AFC, measurements (numpy)\n    bpsk_app.py     peers, conversations,\
      \ receipts, HTTP + SSE server\n    chat_ui.html    the browser front end\n\n\
      Encryption is on by default. Keys live in <rx_dir>/<keys_dir>: this node's\n\
      private key (bpsk_keys.py init) and the keys the operator has approved in the\n\
      UI. With my_addr = 0 and peer_addr = 0 (the default) the node joins the mesh:\n\
      it derives its address from its key, picks a free channel, and lists every\n\
      node in range. Setting both gives the r5.4 two-node behaviour.\n\nThis block\
      \ owns none of that logic. It converts PMT to bytes, drives the\nstate machine\
      \ and turns its decisions into messages for the radio blocks.\nr6.1: it has\
      \ NO stream inputs. Everything it measures arrives as short\nsnapshots (Keep\
      \ M in N -> Stream to Tagged Stream -> Tagged Stream to PDU,\nall C++), so nothing\
      \ in the sample path ever waits for Python: the r6.0.1\nnode block consumed\
      \ four symbol streams and the raw receiver samples in\ngeneral_work, was called\
      \ thousands of times a second with a few samples,\nheld the GIL, and when it\
      \ fell behind the backlog reached the radio source.\n\nPorts in\n    rx0..rx3\
      \    PDUs from each channel's deframer: link frames, plus a\n              \
      \  once-a-second statistics PDU (empty payload) - the liveness\n           \
      \     check of that receive chain\n    meas0..3    512 recovered symbols (Costas\
      \ output) of channel k, 10 a\n                second: SNR (EVM) and the constellation\
      \ for the UI\n    iq0..3      4096 samples of channel k before the matched filter,\
      \ 10 a\n                second: channel level (dBFS) and the carrier offset\
      \ (AFC)\n    adc         8192 raw receiver samples, 20 a second: ADC peak, clipping,\n\
      \                spectrum; the input of the gain control\n    txstat      the\
      \ transmit framer's backlog, 20 a second\n    rx_frame    decoded frames from\
      \ a single-receiver flowgraph (r5)\n    chat_in     the GNU Radio console edit\
      \ box\n    tick        Message Strobe, 10 ms\nPorts out\n    tx_frame    link\
      \ frames for the transmit framer (PDU)\n    tx_en       {'enable': bool} for\
      \ the transmit framer\n    tx_ctl      {'inc': rad/sample} for the rotator that\
      \ puts the\n                transmitter on its channel\n    afc0..3     {'inc':\
      \ rad/sample} for each receive channel's rotator\n    rx_attr     {'hardwaregain':\
      \ dB} for the IIO Attribute Sink (RX)\n    tx_attr     {'hardwaregain': -dB}\
      \ for the IIO Attribute Sink (TX)\n    log         console lines\n\nThe chat\
      \ UI is served on 127.0.0.1:<http_port> and, like the stderr tap\nthat counts\
      \ gr-iio's 'O'/'U' marks and the telemetry files, starts on the\nfirst tick\
      \ rather than in __init__: GRC instantiates this block every time\nit validates\
      \ the flowgraph and must not be left holding a socket, a thread\nor a file.\n\
      \"\"\"\n\nimport math\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport time\n\
      import traceback\nfrom collections import deque\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport\
      \ pmt\nfrom gnuradio import gr\n\n\ndef _load(name):\n    \"\"\"Load a sibling\
      \ module by absolute path, never by module name.\n\n    GRC validates this block\
      \ by running exec() on this source in an empty\n    namespace, so there is no\
      \ __file__ and the working directory is wherever\n    GRC was started. Loading\
      \ the file directly makes both irrelevant, and\n    swallowing every failure\
      \ keeps a missing module from painting the block\n    red in the editor - __init__\
      \ reports it on the console instead.\n    \"\"\"\n    import importlib.util\n\
      \n    if name in sys.modules:\n        return sys.modules[name]\n\n    roots\
      \ = []\n    try:\n        roots.append(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n\
      \    except NameError:\n        pass\n    roots.append(os.getcwd())\n    roots.extend([entry\
      \ for entry in sys.path if entry])\n\n    for root in roots:\n        path =\
      \ os.path.join(root, name + '.py')\n        if not os.path.isfile(path):\n \
      \           continue\n        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name,\
      \ path)\n        module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n        sys.modules[name]\
      \ = module\n        try:\n            spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    \
      \    except Exception:\n            sys.modules.pop(name, None)\n          \
      \  raise\n        return module\n    return None\n\n\n_load_error = ''\ntry:\n\
      \    bpsk_link = _load('bpsk_link')\n    for _dep in ('bpsk_crypto', 'bpsk_secure',\
      \ 'bpsk_mac', 'bpsk_gain',\n                 'bpsk_phy'):\n        if bpsk_link\
      \ is not None and _load(_dep) is None:\n            bpsk_link = None\n    bpsk_app\
      \ = _load('bpsk_app') if bpsk_link is not None else None\n    bpsk_phy = sys.modules.get('bpsk_phy')\n\
      \    if bpsk_app is None:\n        _load_error = ('bpsk_link.py / bpsk_crypto.py\
      \ / bpsk_secure.py / '\n                       'bpsk_mac.py / bpsk_gain.py /\
      \ bpsk_phy.py / '\n                       'bpsk_app.py not found next to the\
      \ flowgraph')\nexcept Exception as _err:            # noqa: BLE001 - reported,\
      \ never raised\n    bpsk_link = bpsk_app = bpsk_phy = None\n    _load_error\
      \ = repr(_err)\n\n\ndef _to_text(msg):\n    \"\"\"Accept whatever the QT edit\
      \ box emits and return a str.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        if pmt.is_symbol(msg):\n\
      \            return pmt.symbol_to_string(msg)\n        if pmt.is_pair(msg):\n\
      \            val = pmt.cdr(msg)\n            if pmt.is_u8vector(val):\n    \
      \            return bytes(bytearray(pmt.u8vector_elements(val))).decode(\n \
      \                   'utf-8', 'replace')\n            if pmt.is_symbol(val):\n\
      \                return pmt.symbol_to_string(val)\n    except Exception:\n \
      \       pass\n    return None\n\n\ndef _to_bytes(msg):\n    \"\"\"Extract the\
      \ u8vector of a PDU as bytes.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        if pmt.is_pair(msg):\n\
      \            val = pmt.cdr(msg)\n            if pmt.is_u8vector(val):\n    \
      \            return bytes(bytearray(pmt.u8vector_elements(val)))\n    except\
      \ Exception:\n        pass\n    return None\n\n\ndef _to_complex(msg):\n   \
      \ \"\"\"The c32vector of a PDU as a numpy array (or None).\"\"\"\n    try:\n\
      \        if pmt.is_pair(msg):\n            val = pmt.cdr(msg)\n            if\
      \ pmt.is_c32vector(val):\n                return np.asarray(pmt.c32vector_elements(val),\n\
      \                                  dtype=np.complex64)\n    except Exception:\n\
      \        pass\n    return None\n\n\ndef _meta(msg):\n    try:\n        if pmt.is_pair(msg)\
      \ and pmt.is_dict(pmt.car(msg)):\n            return pmt.to_python(pmt.car(msg))\
      \ or {}\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return {}\n\n\nNUM_CHANNELS\
      \ = 4          # fixed by the flowgraph: four receive chains\nOUT_RATE_SPS =\
      \ 4          # samples per symbol after the channel filters\nSTALL = 3.0   \
      \            # seconds without data that make a chain 'stalled'\n# snapshot\
      \ taps in the flowgraph (keep m in n): one every n items of\nTAP_EVERY = {'meas':\
      \ 25000,     # symbols (after the Costas loop)\n             'iq': 100000, \
      \     # channel samples (after the AFC rotator)\n             'adc': 300000}\
      \     # radio samples\nCPU_EVERY = 2.0           # seconds between per-thread\
      \ CPU readings\nVIEW_EVERY = 1.0          # seconds between constellation/spectrum\
      \ pushes\n\n\nclass StderrTap(object):\n    \"\"\"Counts gr-iio's overflow 'O'\
      \ / underflow 'U' marks.\n\n    gr-iio writes them with fprintf(stderr, ...)\
      \ from its own overflow and\n    underflow threads, at most one per second per\
      \ direction, so the only\n    place to see them is file descriptor 2. A pipe\
      \ is put there; a thread\n    copies everything to the real stderr unchanged\
      \ and counts the marks\n    (bpsk_phy.count_ou). The pipe is enlarged to 1 MiB\
      \ so writers never\n    block even if this thread is briefly kept from the GIL,\
      \ and any failure\n    puts the original stderr back.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def\
      \ __init__(self):\n        self.overflows = 0\n        self.underflows = 0\n\
      \        self.active = False\n        self.error = None\n        self._orig\
      \ = None\n        self._r = None\n        self._thread = None\n        self._state\
      \ = None\n\n    def start(self):\n        if bpsk_phy is None or self.active:\n\
      \            return\n        try:\n            sys.stderr.flush()\n        \
      \    self._orig = os.dup(2)\n            r, w = os.pipe()\n            try:\n\
      \                import fcntl\n                fcntl.fcntl(w, getattr(fcntl,\
      \ 'F_SETPIPE_SZ', 1031), 1 << 20)\n            except Exception:           \
      \          # noqa: BLE001\n                pass\n            os.dup2(w, 2)\n\
      \            os.close(w)\n            self._r = r\n            self.active =\
      \ True\n            self._thread = threading.Thread(target=self._run, daemon=True,\n\
      \                                            name='bpsk-stderr-tap')\n     \
      \       self._thread.start()\n        except Exception as exc:             \
      \     # noqa: BLE001\n            self.error = repr(exc)\n            self._restore()\n\
      \n    def _run(self):\n        try:\n            while True:\n             \
      \   data = os.read(self._r, 65536)\n                if not data:\n         \
      \           break\n                os.write(self._orig, data)\n            \
      \    o, u, self._state = bpsk_phy.count_ou(\n                    data.decode('latin-1'),\
      \ self._state)\n                self.overflows += o\n                self.underflows\
      \ += u\n        except Exception as exc:                  # noqa: BLE001\n \
      \           self.error = repr(exc)\n        finally:\n            self._restore()\n\
      \n    def _restore(self):\n        if self._orig is not None:\n            try:\n\
      \                os.dup2(self._orig, 2)\n            except OSError:\n     \
      \           pass\n        self.active = False\n\n    def stop(self):\n     \
      \   if not self.active:\n            return\n        self._restore()       \
      \        # writers now go to the real stderr\n        try:\n            os.close(self._r)\
      \         # the reader thread sees EOF/EBADF\n        except OSError:\n    \
      \        pass\n        if self._thread is not None:\n            self._thread.join(timeout=0.5)\n\
      \        try:\n            os.close(self._orig)\n        except OSError:\n \
      \           pass\n        self._orig = None\n\n\ndef _thread_cpu():\n    \"\"\
      \"{tid: (name, cpu seconds)} of this process's threads (Linux).\"\"\"\n    out\
      \ = {}\n    tick = float(os.sysconf('SC_CLK_TCK'))\n    base = '/proc/self/task'\n\
      \    try:\n        tids = os.listdir(base)\n    except OSError:\n        return\
      \ out\n    for tid in tids:\n        try:\n            with open('%s/%s/stat'\
      \ % (base, tid)) as fh:\n                st = fh.read()\n            with open('%s/%s/comm'\
      \ % (base, tid)) as fh:\n                name = fh.read().strip()\n        except\
      \ OSError:\n            continue\n        f = st[st.rfind(')') + 2:].split()\n\
      \        out[tid] = (name, (int(f[11]) + int(f[12])) / tick)\n    return out\n\
      \n\nclass blk(gr.basic_block):\n    \"\"\"BPSK network node: MAC, ARQ link layer,\
      \ encryption, chat UI.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, my_addr=0, peer_addr=0,\
      \ ack_timeout=0.5, max_retries=5,\n                 frag_size=256, queue_ahead=0.03,\
      \ sym_rate=250000.0,\n                 overhead=140, rx_dir='.', nickname='',\
      \ http_port=8088,\n                 open_ui=True, center_freq=0.0, security=True,\n\
      \                 keys_dir='keys', window=32, channel=-1, ch_spacing=600e3,\n\
      \                 ch_first=450e3, radio_rate=6e6, rx_gain=30, tx_atten=50,\n\
      \                 agc=True, telemetry=True, plan_file='', count_ou=True):\n\
      \        gr.basic_block.__init__(self, name='BPSK Chat Node', in_sig=None,\n\
      \                                out_sig=None)\n        self.http_port = int(http_port)\n\
      \        self.open_ui = bool(open_ui)\n        self.radio_rate = float(radio_rate)\n\
      \        self.ch_rate = OUT_RATE_SPS * float(sym_rate)\n        # a chain is\
      \ stalled after STALL s without data, or four snapshot\n        # intervals\
      \ when those are longer (slowed-down bench)\n        self.stall = max(STALL,\
      \ 4.0 * max(\n            TAP_EVERY['meas'] / float(sym_rate),\n           \
      \ TAP_EVERY['iq'] / self.ch_rate,\n            TAP_EVERY['adc'] / self.radio_rate))\n\
      \        self.app = None\n        self.link = None\n        if bpsk_app is None:\n\
      \            print('[chat] ERROR: could not load the protocol modules: %s'\n\
      \                  % _load_error, flush=True)\n        else:\n            root\
      \ = os.path.abspath(rx_dir or '.')\n            store = os.path.join(root, 'chat_files')\n\
      \            chan = int(channel)\n            self.app = bpsk_app.ChatApp(\n\
      \                my_addr=int(my_addr) or None, peer_addr=int(peer_addr) or None,\n\
      \                nick=nickname or None, store_dir=store,\n                ack_timeout=ack_timeout,\
      \ max_retries=max_retries,\n                frag_size=frag_size, queue_ahead=queue_ahead,\n\
      \                sym_rate=sym_rate, overhead=overhead,\n                tx_freq=center_freq,\
      \ rx_freq=center_freq,\n                security=bool(security),\n         \
      \       keys_dir=os.path.join(root, keys_dir or 'keys'),\n                window=int(window),\n\
      \                channel=chan if 0 <= chan < NUM_CHANNELS else None,\n     \
      \           num_channels=NUM_CHANNELS, ch_spacing=float(ch_spacing),\n     \
      \           ch_first=float(ch_first), filler='keepalive',\n                gain=dict(rx_gain=rx_gain,\
      \ tx_atten=tx_atten,\n                          auto=bool(agc)),\n         \
      \       telemetry_dir=(os.path.join(root, 'telemetry')\n                   \
      \            if telemetry else None),\n                plan_file=(os.path.join(root,\
      \ plan_file)\n                           if plan_file else None))\n        \
      \    self.link = self.app.link\n\n        # GNU Radio's Python gateway looks\
      \ a handler up BY NAME on the block\n        # (set_msg_handler passes handler.__name__\
      \ to C++), so every port\n        # needs a real method - a lambda or partial\
      \ aborts the flowgraph.\n        handlers = [('chat_in', self._on_chat), ('rx_frame',\
      \ self._on_rx),\n                    ('tick', self._on_tick), ('adc', self._on_adc),\n\
      \                    ('txstat', self._on_txstat)]\n        for k in range(NUM_CHANNELS):\n\
      \            handlers += [('rx%d' % k, getattr(self, '_on_rx%d' % k)),\n   \
      \                      ('meas%d' % k, getattr(self, '_on_meas%d' % k)),\n  \
      \                       ('iq%d' % k, getattr(self, '_on_iq%d' % k))]\n     \
      \   for port, fn in handlers:\n            self.message_port_register_in(pmt.intern(port))\n\
      \            self.set_msg_handler(pmt.intern(port), fn)\n        outs = ['tx_frame',\
      \ 'tx_en', 'tx_ctl', 'rx_attr', 'tx_attr', 'log'] \\\n            + ['afc%d'\
      \ % k for k in range(NUM_CHANNELS)]\n        for port in outs:\n           \
      \ self.message_port_register_out(pmt.intern(port))\n\n        self._lock = threading.RLock()\n\
      \        self._last_strobe = 0.0\n        self._watchdog = None\n        self._server\
      \ = None\n        self._opened = False\n        # Set by stop(). Everything\
      \ that can touch a message port or acquire a\n        # resource checks it first:\
      \ after stop() the runtime is tearing the\n        # block down, and publishing\
      \ to a port from a Python thread at that\n        # point is a call into freed\
      \ C++.\n        self._halt = threading.Event()\n        self._faults = 0\n \
      \       # Interned once; _dispatch runs up to 100 times a second.\n        self._port_log\
      \ = pmt.intern('log')\n        self._port_tx = pmt.intern('tx_frame')\n    \
      \    self._port_en = pmt.intern('tx_en')\n        self._port_ctl = pmt.intern('tx_ctl')\n\
      \        self._port_rxa = pmt.intern('rx_attr')\n        self._port_txa = pmt.intern('tx_attr')\n\
      \        self._port_afc = [pmt.intern('afc%d' % k) for k in range(NUM_CHANNELS)]\n\
      \        self._k_inc = pmt.intern('inc')\n        self._k_en = pmt.intern('enable')\n\
      \        self._k_gain = pmt.intern('hardwaregain')\n        # Physical-layer\
      \ state (r6.1).\n        self._afc = ([bpsk_phy.Afc(self.ch_rate) for _ in range(NUM_CHANNELS)]\n\
      \                     if bpsk_phy is not None else [])\n        self._lvl =\
      \ [None] * NUM_CHANNELS          # (t, dBFS) per channel\n        self._lvl_push\
      \ = 0.0\n        self._seen = {'meas': [0.0] * NUM_CHANNELS, 'iq': [0.0] * NUM_CHANNELS,\n\
      \                      'dfr': [0.0] * NUM_CHANNELS, 'adc': 0.0}\n        self._dfr\
      \ = [None] * NUM_CHANNELS\n        self._dfr_bits = [None] * NUM_CHANNELS\n\
      \        self._fault = None\n        self._fault_told = -1e9\n        self._started\
      \ = None\n        self._disp = deque()                       # (serial, airtime)\
      \ sent\n        self._serial = 0\n        self._txq = {}\n        self._tap\
      \ = StderrTap() if count_ou else None\n        self._cpu_prev = None\n     \
      \   self._cpu_next = 0.0\n        self._view = {'const': [None] * NUM_CHANNELS,\
      \ 'spectrum': None}\n        self._view_next = 0.0\n        if self.link is\
      \ not None:\n            self._say(self.app.banner())\n            if self.app.plan_note:\n\
      \                self._say(self.app.plan_note)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\
      \ plumbing\n    def _say(self, text):\n        for line in str(text).splitlines():\n\
      \            print('[link] %s' % line, flush=True)\n        if self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \            return\n        self.message_port_pub(self._port_log, pmt.string_to_symbol(str(text)))\n\
      \n    def _inc(self, offset_hz, rate):\n        return pmt.dict_add(pmt.make_dict(),\
      \ self._k_inc,\n                            pmt.from_double(2.0 * math.pi *\
      \ offset_hz / rate))\n\n    def _dispatch(self, actions):\n        if self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \            return\n        for kind, value in actions:\n            if kind\
      \ == 'tx':\n                vec = pmt.init_u8vector(len(value), list(bytearray(value)))\n\
      \                self.message_port_pub(self._port_tx, pmt.cons(pmt.PMT_NIL,\
      \ vec))\n                self._serial += 1\n                self._disp.append((self._serial,\n\
      \                                   self.link.radio.airtime(len(value))))\n\
      \                while len(self._disp) > 4096:\n                    self._disp.popleft()\n\
      \            elif kind == 'chan':\n                # Retune the transmitter:\
      \ the rotator after the modulator.\n                # Receive is untouched (all\
      \ channels).\n                self.message_port_pub(self._port_ctl, self._inc(\n\
      \                    float(self.app.offset(value)), self.radio_rate))\n    \
      \        elif kind == 'txen':\n                self.message_port_pub(self._port_en,\
      \ pmt.dict_add(\n                    pmt.make_dict(), self._k_en, pmt.from_bool(bool(value))))\n\
      \            elif kind == 'gain':\n                # IIO Attribute Sinks; bpsk_gain\
      \ keeps the values in range,\n                # which matters: attr_sink throws\
      \ on a refused write.\n                v = int(value['value'])\n           \
      \     port = self._port_rxa if value['what'] == 'rx' \\\n                  \
      \  else self._port_txa\n                text = str(v if value['what'] == 'rx'\
      \ else -v)\n                self.message_port_pub(port, pmt.dict_add(\n    \
      \                pmt.make_dict(), self._k_gain, pmt.intern(text)))\n       \
      \     elif kind == 'log':\n                self._say(value)\n\n    def _fault_tb(self,\
      \ where):\n        self._faults += 1\n        n = self._faults\n        if n\
      \ <= 5 or n % 1000 == 0:\n            print('[chat] INTERNAL ERROR #%d in %s\
      \ - that input was discarded, '\n                  'the node keeps running:'\
      \ % (n, where), flush=True)\n            traceback.print_exc()\n           \
      \ sys.stdout.flush()\n            sys.stderr.flush()\n            if n == 5:\n\
      \                print('[chat] further tracebacks are printed every 1000th '\n\
      \                      'fault only', flush=True)\n            try:\n       \
      \         self._say('internal error in %s (#%d) - traceback on the '\n     \
      \                     'terminal' % (where, n))\n            except Exception:\n\
      \                pass\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\
      \ startup\n    def _ensure_running(self):\n        \"\"\"Start the UI server,\
      \ the fallback timer and the stderr tap on first\n        traffic. Deferred\
      \ out of __init__ so that GRC, which instantiates this\n        block every\
      \ time it validates the flowgraph, never binds the port,\n        spawns a thread\
      \ or redirects a file descriptor.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.app is None\
      \ or self._halt.is_set():\n            return\n        if self._started is None:\n\
      \            self._started = time.time()\n            if self._tap is not None:\n\
      \                self._tap.start()\n            # gr-iio's Pluto source template\
      \ never applies its RF bandwidth\n            # parameter (3.10), so the receiver's\
      \ analog filter is whatever\n            # the device had. Set it for the channel\
      \ plan: 0.9 x the rate.\n            bw = int(max(2e5, min(5.6e7, 0.9 * self.radio_rate)))\n\
      \            self.message_port_pub(self._port_rxa, pmt.dict_add(\n         \
      \       pmt.make_dict(), pmt.intern('rf_bandwidth'),\n                pmt.intern(str(bw))))\n\
      \        if self._server is None:\n            try:\n                self._server,\
      \ _ = bpsk_app.serve(self.app, self.http_port)\n                url = 'http://127.0.0.1:%d/'\
      \ % self.http_port\n                self._say('chat UI ready at %s  (files in\
      \ %s)'\n                          % (url, self.app.store_dir))\n           \
      \     if self.open_ui and not self._opened:\n                    self._opened\
      \ = True\n                    threading.Thread(target=self._open_browser, args=(url,),\n\
      \                                     daemon=True).start()\n            except\
      \ OSError as exc:\n                self._server = False        # do not retry\
      \ every 10 ms\n                self._say('could not start the chat UI on port\
      \ %d: %s'\n                          % (self.http_port, exc))\n        if self._watchdog\
      \ is None:\n            self._watchdog = threading.Thread(target=self._watchdog_loop,\n\
      \                                              daemon=True)\n            self._watchdog.start()\n\
      \n    @staticmethod\n    def _open_browser(url):\n        import webbrowser\n\
      \        time.sleep(0.7)\n        try:\n            webbrowser.open(url)\n \
      \       except Exception:\n            pass\n\n    def stop(self):\n       \
      \ \"\"\"Stop the watchdog and release the port, in that order.\n\n        Order\
      \ matters. The watchdog drives on_tick and publishes the frames it\n       \
      \ produces; left running it keeps calling message_port_pub while the\n     \
      \   runtime destroys the block. Because stop() also freezes _last_strobe,\n\
      \        the watchdog ENGAGES within 250 ms of teardown and then publishes at\n\
      \        100 Hz, so this is the steady state during shutdown, not a rare race.\n\
      \        \"\"\"\n        self._halt.set()\n        watchdog, self._watchdog\
      \ = self._watchdog, None\n        if watchdog is not None and watchdog.is_alive():\n\
      \            watchdog.join(timeout=1.0)\n        server, self._server = self._server,\
      \ None\n        if server:\n            bpsk_app.shutdown(server)\n        if\
      \ self._tap is not None:\n            self._tap.stop()\n        if self.app\
      \ is not None:\n            self.app.close()\n        return True\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\
      \ message ports\n    def _watchdog_loop(self):\n        \"\"\"Drive on_tick\
      \ if the Message Strobe stops delivering.\n\n        Every ARQ timer and the\
      \ beacons hang off the tick port. If that port\n        goes quiet the link\
      \ silently wedges: nothing retransmits and the queue\n        never drains.\
      \ This takes over after 250 ms of silence and stands down\n        if the strobe\
      \ returns.\n        \"\"\"\n        engaged = False\n        while not self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \            if self._halt.wait(0.01):\n                return             \
      \         # stop() asked us to leave\n            try:\n                with\
      \ self._lock:\n                    if self.app is None or self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \                        continue\n                    if (time.time() - self._last_strobe)\
      \ < 0.25:\n                        if engaged:\n                           \
      \ engaged = False\n                            self._say('message strobe recovered,\
      \ watchdog '\n                                      'standing down')\n     \
      \                   continue\n                    if not engaged:\n        \
      \                engaged = True\n                        self._say('WARNING:\
      \ no tick from the Message Strobe '\n                                  'block\
      \ - driving ARQ timers and beacons '\n                                  'from\
      \ the fallback thread instead')\n                    self._dispatch(self.app.on_tick(time.time()))\n\
      \            except Exception:\n                self._fault_tb('watchdog')\n\
      \n    def _on_chat(self, msg):\n        if self.app is None or self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \            return\n        text = _to_text(msg)\n        if text is None:\n\
      \            return\n        try:\n            with self._lock:\n          \
      \      self._ensure_running()\n                self._dispatch(self.app.on_console(text,\
      \ time.time()))\n        except Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('chat_in')\n\
      \n    def _on_rx(self, msg, channel=None):\n        if self.app is None or self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \            return\n        raw = _to_bytes(msg)\n        if raw is None:\n\
      \            return\n        try:\n            with self._lock:\n          \
      \      self._ensure_running()\n                now = time.time()\n         \
      \       if not raw:\n                    meta = _meta(msg)\n               \
      \     if channel is not None and 'stats' in meta:\n                        self._on_deframer_stats(channel,\
      \ meta['stats'], now)\n                    return\n                self._dispatch(self.app.on_rx(raw,\
      \ now, channel=channel))\n        except Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('rx_frame'\
      \ if channel is None else 'rx%d' % channel)\n\n    def _on_rx0(self, msg):\n\
      \        self._on_rx(msg, 0)\n\n    def _on_rx1(self, msg):\n        self._on_rx(msg,\
      \ 1)\n\n    def _on_rx2(self, msg):\n        self._on_rx(msg, 2)\n\n    def\
      \ _on_rx3(self, msg):\n        self._on_rx(msg, 3)\n\n    def _on_meas0(self,\
      \ msg):\n        self._on_meas(msg, 0)\n\n    def _on_meas1(self, msg):\n  \
      \      self._on_meas(msg, 1)\n\n    def _on_meas2(self, msg):\n        self._on_meas(msg,\
      \ 2)\n\n    def _on_meas3(self, msg):\n        self._on_meas(msg, 3)\n\n   \
      \ def _on_iq0(self, msg):\n        self._on_iq(msg, 0)\n\n    def _on_iq1(self,\
      \ msg):\n        self._on_iq(msg, 1)\n\n    def _on_iq2(self, msg):\n      \
      \  self._on_iq(msg, 2)\n\n    def _on_iq3(self, msg):\n        self._on_iq(msg,\
      \ 3)\n\n    def _on_tick(self, msg):\n        if self.app is None or self._halt.is_set():\n\
      \            return\n        try:\n            with self._lock:\n          \
      \      now = time.time()\n                self._last_strobe = now\n        \
      \        self._ensure_running()\n                self._push_levels(now)\n  \
      \              self._dispatch(self.app.on_tick(now))\n                self._housekeeping(now)\n\
      \        except Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('tick')\n\n    # -------------------------------------------------\
      \ physical layer (r6.1)\n    def _on_meas(self, msg, k):\n        \"\"\"Recovered\
      \ symbols of channel k: SNR from the EVM (decisions on\n        the real axis,\
      \ which is what a locked differential BPSK receiver\n        produces after\
      \ the Costas loop), and the constellation for the UI.\"\"\"\n        if self.app\
      \ is None or self._halt.is_set() or bpsk_phy is None:\n            return\n\
      \        try:\n            x = _to_complex(msg)\n            if x is None or\
      \ not len(x):\n                return\n            now = time.time()\n     \
      \       self._seen['meas'][k] = now\n            snr, evm = bpsk_phy.evm_snr(x)\n\
      \            with self._lock:\n                if snr is None:\n           \
      \         self.app.set_radio_metrics(snr_db=None, evm=None,\n              \
      \                                 locked=False, channel=k)\n               \
      \ else:\n                    self.app.set_radio_metrics(\n                 \
      \       snr_db=round(snr, 2), evm=round(100.0 * evm, 2),\n                 \
      \       locked=bool(snr > 5.0), channel=k)\n            if now >= self._view_next\
      \ - 0.5:\n                pts = x[:96]\n                self._view['const'][k]\
      \ = [[round(float(z.real), 2),\n                                           round(float(z.imag),\
      \ 2)]\n                                          for z in pts]\n        except\
      \ Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('meas%d' % k)\n\n    def _on_iq(self,\
      \ msg, k):\n        \"\"\"Channel k before the matched filter: its in-band level\
      \ relative\n        to ADC full scale (the channel filters have unity gain;\
      \ the level is\n        taken after a matched filter, so it is what the decoder\
      \ sees) and\n        the AFC.\"\"\"\n        if self.app is None or self._halt.is_set()\
      \ or bpsk_phy is None:\n            return\n        try:\n            x = _to_complex(msg)\n\
      \            if x is None or not len(x):\n                return\n         \
      \   now = time.time()\n            self._seen['iq'][k] = now\n            lvl\
      \ = bpsk_phy.inband_level_db(x)\n            self._lvl[k] = (now, round(lvl,\
      \ 1))\n            with self._lock:\n                self.app.set_radio_metrics(level_db=round(lvl,\
      \ 1), channel=k)\n            afc = self._afc[k]\n            inc = afc.update(now,\
      \ x)\n            if inc is not None and not self._halt.is_set():\n        \
      \        self.message_port_pub(self._port_afc[k], pmt.dict_add(\n          \
      \          pmt.make_dict(), self._k_inc, pmt.from_double(inc)))\n        except\
      \ Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('iq%d' % k)\n\n    def _on_adc(self,\
      \ msg):\n        \"\"\"Raw receiver samples: ADC peak and clipping (the gain\
      \ control's\n        input), and a spectrum for the UI.\"\"\"\n        if self.app\
      \ is None or self._halt.is_set() or bpsk_phy is None:\n            return\n\
      \        try:\n            x = _to_complex(msg)\n            if x is None or\
      \ not len(x):\n                return\n            now = time.time()\n     \
      \       self._seen['adc'] = now\n            st = bpsk_phy.adc_stats(x)\n  \
      \          with self._lock:\n                self.app.set_adc(peak_dbfs=round(st['peak_dbfs'],\
      \ 1),\n                                 rms_dbfs=round(st['rms_dbfs'], 1),\n\
      \                                 clip=st['clip'], t=now)\n            if now\
      \ >= self._view_next - 0.5 and self._view['spectrum'] is None:\n           \
      \     self._view['spectrum'] = bpsk_phy.spectrum_db(x, 128)\n        except\
      \ Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('adc')\n\n    def _on_txstat(self,\
      \ msg):\n        \"\"\"The transmit framer's report: correct the airtime model.\"\
      \"\"\n        if self.app is None or self._halt.is_set():\n            return\n\
      \        try:\n            st = pmt.to_python(msg) if pmt.is_dict(msg) else\
      \ None\n            if not st:\n                return\n            received\
      \ = (st.get('accepted', 0) + st.get('dropped', 0)\n                        +\
      \ st.get('rejected', 0))\n            while self._disp and self._disp[0][0]\
      \ <= received:\n                self._disp.popleft()\n            pending =\
      \ sum(a for _, a in self._disp)\n            now = time.time()\n           \
      \ with self._lock:\n                if st.get('enabled') and st.get('backlog')\
      \ is not None:\n                    self.link.radio.observe(\n             \
      \           now, float(st['t']) + float(st['backlog']) + pending)\n        \
      \        self._txq = {'backlog': st.get('backlog'),\n                      \
      \       'dropped': st.get('dropped', 0),\n                             'flushed':\
      \ st.get('flushed', 0),\n                             'enabled': bool(st.get('enabled')),\n\
      \                             'sent': st.get('sent', 0),\n                 \
      \            'fill_bits': st.get('fill_bits', 0),\n                        \
      \     'model_error': self.link.radio.model_error,\n                        \
      \     'error': st.get('error')}\n        except Exception:\n            self._fault_tb('txstat')\n\
      \n    def _on_deframer_stats(self, k, stats, now):\n        if not isinstance(stats,\
      \ dict):\n            return\n        bits = stats.get('bits')\n        if bits\
      \ is not None and bits != self._dfr_bits[k]:\n            self._seen['dfr'][k]\
      \ = now\n        self._dfr_bits[k] = bits\n        self._dfr[k] = stats\n\n\
      \    def _push_levels(self, now):\n        \"\"\"One level per channel, all\
      \ from the last 0.3 s, ten times a\n        second: the MAC's energy detection\
      \ compares them with each other.\"\"\"\n        if now - self._lvl_push < 0.1:\n\
      \            return\n        self._lvl_push = now\n        lv = [(v[1] if v\
      \ is not None and now - v[0] < 0.3 else None)\n              for v in self._lvl]\n\
      \        if any(x is not None for x in lv):\n            self.app.set_channel_levels(lv,\
      \ now)\n\n    def _housekeeping(self, now):\n        \"\"\"Liveness, counters,\
      \ CPU and UI snapshots (all cheap; every tick).\"\"\"\n        started = self._started\
      \ or now\n        warm = now - started > self.stall + 2.0\n        adc_age =\
      \ now - self._seen['adc'] if self._seen['adc'] else None\n        chans = []\n\
      \        for k in range(NUM_CHANNELS):\n            last = min(self._seen['meas'][k],\
      \ self._seen['dfr'][k])\n            chans.append(bool(last) and now - last\
      \ < self.stall)\n        fault = None\n        if warm and (adc_age is None\
      \ or adc_age > self.stall):\n            fault = ('receiver stalled: no samples\
      \ from the radio for more '\n                     'than %.0f s - check the E200\
      \ link (USB/Ethernet) and '\n                     'the console' % self.stall)\n\
      \        elif warm and not all(chans):\n            dead = [k for k in range(NUM_CHANNELS)\
      \ if not chans[k]]\n            fault = ('receive chain of channel%s %s stalled\
      \ (no data for '\n                     'more than %.0f s)%s'\n             \
      \        % ('s' if len(dead) > 1 else '',\n                        ', '.join(str(k)\
      \ for k in dead), self.stall,\n                        '; the other channels\
      \ are unaffected'\n                        if len(dead) < NUM_CHANNELS else\
      \ ''))\n        if fault != self._fault:\n            self._fault = fault\n\
      \            if fault:\n                self._fault_told = now\n           \
      \     self._say('FAULT: ' + fault)\n                self.app._system(fault,\
      \ 'error')\n            elif warm:\n                self._say('receive chains\
      \ running again')\n        elif fault and now - self._fault_told > 30.0:\n \
      \           self._fault_told = now\n            self._say('FAULT (continuing):\
      \ ' + fault)\n        self.app.set_phy('live', {'channels': chans, 'fault':\
      \ fault,\n                                  'adc_age': adc_age})\n        tap\
      \ = self._tap\n        self.app.set_phy('ou', {'overflows': tap.overflows if\
      \ tap else None,\n                                'underflows': tap.underflows\
      \ if tap else None,\n                                'tap': bool(tap and tap.active),\n\
      \                                'error': tap.error if tap else None})\n   \
      \     self.app.set_phy('afc', [{'cfo': round(a.cfo, 1),\n                  \
      \                'residual': (round(a.residual, 1)\n                       \
      \                        if a.residual is not None\n                       \
      \                        else None),\n                                  'ratio':\
      \ round(a.ratio, 1),\n                                  'updates': a.updates}\
      \ for a in self._afc])\n        self.app.set_phy('deframer', list(self._dfr))\n\
      \        self.app.set_phy('txq', dict(self._txq))\n        if now >= self._cpu_next:\n\
      \            self._cpu_next = now + CPU_EVERY\n            self._sample_cpu(now)\n\
      \        if now >= self._view_next:\n            self._view_next = now + VIEW_EVERY\n\
      \            self.app.publish_view(dict(self._view))\n            self._view\
      \ = {'const': [None] * NUM_CHANNELS, 'spectrum': None}\n\n    def _sample_cpu(self,\
      \ now):\n        \"\"\"CPU per GNU Radio thread (threads carry their block's\
      \ name).\"\"\"\n        snap = _thread_cpu()\n        proc = sum(os.times()[:2])\n\
      \        prev, self._cpu_prev = self._cpu_prev, (now, snap, proc)\n        if\
      \ prev is None:\n            return\n        dt = max(1e-3, now - prev[0])\n\
      \        agg = {}\n        for tid, (name, c) in snap.items():\n           \
      \ old = prev[1].get(tid)\n            if old is None:\n                continue\n\
      \            key = name.rstrip('0123456789') or name\n            agg[key] =\
      \ agg.get(key, 0.0) + (c - old[1]) / dt\n        top = sorted(agg.items(), key=lambda\
      \ kv: -kv[1])[:12]\n        self.app.set_phy('cpu', {'process': round((proc\
      \ - prev[2]) / dt, 2),\n                                 'top': [[n, round(c,\
      \ 3)] for n, c in top\n                                         if c >= 0.005]})\n"
    ack_timeout: ack_timeout
    affinity: ''
    agc: agc
    alias: ''
